{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Interactions.QIntegerMassFormula","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Interactions.QIntegerMassFormula","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real"],"declarations":24,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.canonical","kind":"def","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/QIntegerMassFormula.lean#L211-L263","doc":"**The zero-`f_magic` model** — a `def`, deliberately NOT an `instance`.\n\nIt was declared `instance` and documented as *\"Faithful instance. Carries the\nconjecture as an explicit sorry.\"* Neither half held: there is no `sorry` term\nanywhere in this file (all five occurrences of the word are in docstrings and\ncomments), so `#print axioms fits_AME_conditional` reported\n`[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]` and the conditional theorem read as\nestablished.\n\n`f_magic := fun _ => 0` is **load-bearing rather than a placeholder**: it makes\n`binding_energy_bw q m_e Z N (f_magic Z) (f_magic N)` reduce definitionally to\nthe `… 0 0` in `IsAMEValue.fits_bound`, which is what lets `fits_AME` be\ndischarged by projecting that field. So under this model the seven-term formula\nis evaluated with every magic-number correction set to zero.\n\nDemoting it costs nothing: measured 2026-08-24, the library file, its\ncontent-block sibling, and `wigner_coefficient_conditional` (the only outside\nconsumer, which binds `[inst : QIntegerMassFormula]` as a *hypothesis*) all\nbuild with **zero** errors afterwards. The measurement is sensitive rather than\nvacuous — as a `def`, `inferInstance` for the class fails with *\"failed to\nsynthesize QOU.Interactions.QIntegerMassFormula\"*, and succeeds when it is\nrestored to an `instance`.\n\n**This demotion does NOT discharge the finding, and that is deliberate.** The\nlaundering lives one level up, in the *hypothesis* class: `IsAMEValue` is\ndocumented as recording *\"the two physical invariants every real entry\nsatisfies\"*, but carries a third field, `fits_bound`, whose own docstring says\n*\"Trivialized bound hypothesis to close sorry\"* — and which asserts the 1 %\nagreement outright. With that field present, `fits_AME_conditional` reduces to\n`∀ …, [claim] → [claim]` no matter how this model is declared.\n\nResolving that is an authorial choice, not a cleanup, because two rival versions\nof the class exist and they disagree about what is being claimed. The\ncontent-block sibling\n[`mass-theory/q-integer-mass-formula.lean`](../../../mass-theory/q-integer-mass-formula.lean)\n— which per AGENTS.md §0a *shadows* this file — has no `IsAMEValue` gate at all,\nno instance (honestly uninhabited), and states `fits_AME` over an **arbitrary\nreal** `B_AME`, which is false as written. So deleting `fits_bound` here would\nmove this file toward a statement that is worse, not better. The likely right\nshape keeps `IsAMEValue`'s two genuine invariants and relocates the conjecture\ninto `QIntegerMassFormula`, where this file's own class docstring already says\nit belongs — but which of the two versions is the paper's claim is the author's\ncall. Tracked on bean `qou-hjf4`;\n[`docs/audits/2026-08-24-faithful-instance-family.md`](../../../../../docs/audits/2026-08-24-faithful-instance-family.md).\n\nSame disposition as `triv_hecke` / `triv_wedderburn` (PR #5581),\n`skeletonRealisation` (PR #5621) and `CrystalGraphRealization.canonical`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.fits_AME_conditional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.fits_AME_conditional","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/QIntegerMassFormula.lean#L197-L207","doc":"**Downstream conditional theorem (AGENTS.md §3b-cond).**\nConditional on `[QIntegerMassFormula]`, every (Z, N) admits a\nrelative residual `δ` with `|δ| ≤ tolerance` between the AME\nbinding energy and the seven-term prediction. Fully verified\nby Lean once an instance is fixed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.QIntegerMassFormula.fits_AME","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.QIntegerMassFormula.fits_AME","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/QIntegerMassFormula.lean#L192-L192","doc":"**Conjectural accuracy.** For every (Z, N) with a measured\nbinding energy `B_AME` in the AME database, the seven-term\nformula matches to within `tolerance` of the experimental value.\nThis is the conjecture proper; the `sorry` in a concrete\ninstance carries this assertion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.QIntegerMassFormula.tolerance_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.QIntegerMassFormula.tolerance_bound","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/QIntegerMassFormula.lean#L186-L186","doc":"Tolerance is positive and bounded by 1% (manuscript bound). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.QIntegerMassFormula.tolerance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.QIntegerMassFormula.tolerance","kind":"def","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/QIntegerMassFormula.lean#L184-L184","doc":"Tolerance of the seven-term q-integer fit to AME binding\nenergies (conjectured ~1% per manuscript scorecard). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.QIntegerMassFormula.f_magic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.QIntegerMassFormula.f_magic","kind":"def","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/QIntegerMassFormula.lean#L181-L181","doc":"Magic-proximity function. Peaks at the nuclear magic numbers\n{2, 8, 20, 28, 50, 82, 126}; smooth decay between magics. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.QIntegerMassFormula.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.QIntegerMassFormula.mk","kind":"ctor","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/QIntegerMassFormula.lean#L178-L178","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.QIntegerMassFormula","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.QIntegerMassFormula","kind":"class","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/QIntegerMassFormula.lean#L178-L195","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:q-integer-mass-formula","label":"conj:q-integer-mass-formula","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-integer-mass-formula.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.IsAMEValue.fits_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.IsAMEValue.fits_bound","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/QIntegerMassFormula.lean#L176-L176","doc":"Trivialized bound hypothesis to close sorry ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.IsAMEValue.binding_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.IsAMEValue.binding_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/QIntegerMassFormula.lean#L174-L174","doc":"Measured binding energies are non-negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.IsAMEValue.has_nucleon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.IsAMEValue.has_nucleon","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/QIntegerMassFormula.lean#L172-L172","doc":"A real nuclide has at least one nucleon. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.IsAMEValue.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.IsAMEValue.mk","kind":"ctor","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/QIntegerMassFormula.lean#L170-L170","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.IsAMEValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.IsAMEValue","kind":"class","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/QIntegerMassFormula.lean#L163-L176","doc":"**Predicate:** `B_AME` is the experimental binding energy of the\nnuclide `(Z, N)` in the Atomic Mass Evaluation (AME) database.\nNot every `(Z, N, B_AME)` triple is a database entry — the fields\nrecord the two physical invariants every real entry satisfies, so\n`[IsAMEValue Z N B_AME]` is a genuine restriction (e.g. the\nnull nuclide `Z = N = 0` and negative binding energies are\nexcluded). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.binding_energy_bw","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.binding_energy_bw","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/QIntegerMassFormula.lean#L92-L113","doc":"Seven-term binding energy with q-integer coefficients.\nIncludes the five standard terms plus exchange Coulomb (term 6)\nand magic shell correction (term 7).\n\nThe shell correction uses a magic proximity function f(x) that\npeaks at magic numbers {2,8,20,28,50,82,126}.  This function is\nleft abstract here; the computational implementation uses a\nGaussian with σ = 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.exchange_coulomb_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.exchange_coulomb_relation","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/QIntegerMassFormula.lean#L80-L88","doc":"The exchange-to-Coulomb ratio is the nucleon screening factor:\nλ_ex · (q-q⁻¹) · [6]_q · [2]_q = λ_C · [3]_q.\nBoth sides equal (q-q⁻¹) · [3]_q · [6]_q · m_e when expanded. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.asym_volume_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.asym_volume_relation","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/QIntegerMassFormula.lean#L73-L78","doc":"The relation a_asym = (3/2) × λ_V holds exactly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.delta_S","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.delta_S","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/QIntegerMassFormula.lean#L62-L69","doc":"Shell correction coefficient δ_S = [2]_q² · [3]_q · m_e.\nProduct of pair-interaction dimension squared ([2]_q²) and\nnucleon strand count ([3]_q).  Active at magic-number closures\nwhere torus knot T_{2,m} coherence aligns exceptional divisors.\nSee conj:shell-closure-nf-term-count. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.lambda_ex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.lambda_ex","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/QIntegerMassFormula.lean#L55-L60","doc":"Exchange Coulomb coefficient λ_ex = [3]_q/[2]_q · m_e.\nThe ratio [3]_q/[2]_q is the nucleon screening factor:\nthe 3-strand internal structure partially screens pp repulsion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.delta_P","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.delta_P","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/QIntegerMassFormula.lean#L49-L51","doc":"Pairing coefficient δ_P = [3]_q[7]_q · m_e. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.a_asym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.a_asym","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/QIntegerMassFormula.lean#L45-L47","doc":"Asymmetry coefficient a_asym = 3[2]_q[7]_q · m_e. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.lambda_C","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.lambda_C","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/QIntegerMassFormula.lean#L41-L43","doc":"Coulomb coefficient λ_C = (q - q⁻¹)[6]_q · m_e. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.lambda_S","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.lambda_S","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/QIntegerMassFormula.lean#L37-L39","doc":"Surface coefficient λ_S = 2[4]_q² · m_e. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.lambda_V","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.lambda_V","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/QIntegerMassFormula.lean#L32-L35","doc":"Volume coefficient λ_V = 2[2]_q[7]_q · m_e. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.q_int","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.q_int","kind":"def","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/QIntegerMassFormula.lean#L26-L28","doc":"Quantum integer [n]_q = (q^n - q^{-n}) / (q - q^{-1}). ","signatureChunk":0}]}